# `docs/` ships. `docs/scoring_metric.md` *is* Tranche 3 Deliverable 4, and a
# metric nobody can read is not a metric; the benchmark report is D4.2. Two
# files are held back rather than published stale:
#
#   - the PDF documents `parser.rs` / `lifted_ir.rs`, i.e. the _legacy
#     architecture this workspace replaced. It describes a system that no
#     longer exists.
#   - gap_analysis.md's status block still says score-2.0.0 milestones M5–M7
#     "are not" built (they are, all of them) and links into private `plan/`.
#     It is a real deliverable and should ship — after a refresh, not before.
/docs/soroban_decompiler_docs.pdf
/docs/benchmarks/gap_analysis.md

# Personal sandbox — kept locally for reference but not pushed.
# Test-relevant fixtures live in `samples/contracts/` instead.
/learning/

# CLI output defaults
/out/

# soroban-sdk's test host writes a JSON snapshot of every test's ledger, auth
# and event state next to the crate under test. Useful for eyeballing a probe
# run, but it is regenerated on every invocation and is not a golden file —
# committing it would produce churn on every `--ignored` run. When the harness
# grows real golden files (plan B7) they get an explicit, committed home.
**/test_snapshots/

